/target
# `tools/*` are standalone crates with their own Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock (see
# "Automatic updates" in docs/release.md). The `/target` above is anchored to
# the repo root, so each of theirs has to be named. Their `Cargo.lock` files ARE
# committed — they are binaries, and the release workflow builds them `--locked`.
/tools/*/target
.claude/settings.local.json
# Release archives produced by scripts/package.sh; regenerated, never committed.
/dist
# scripts/generate-icons.py imports scripts/make-icon-master.py as a module, so
# running it leaves a bytecode cache behind. The icon artifacts themselves ARE
# committed (docs/release.md, "Application icon"); only this is not.
__pycache__/
